    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For dyadic m=3h+e with 0<e<h, the reciprocal complement creates a second coefficient gap in Z^(2/3). If h>=2e+1, its order-e differential recurrence propagates backward without a stall because 3 does not divide e. Hence E_h^prim(m,p)=0 whenever 7h>=2m+1, and live exact-level widths satisfy h<=floor(2m/7).",
